# IPv4 Classes
| Class | First Octet Range | Default Subnet Mask | Network Size | Typical Use                    |
| ----- | ----------------: | ------------------- | -----------: | ------------------------------ |
| A     |             1–126 | 255.0.0.0 (/8)      |   Very Large | Large organizations, ISPs      |
| B     |           128–191 | 255.255.0.0 (/16)   |       Medium | Universities, medium companies |
| C     |           192–223 | 255.255.255.0 (/24) |        Small | Homes and small businesses     |
| D     |           224–239 | N/A                 |          N/A | Multicast                      |
| E     |           240–255 | N/A                 |          N/A | Experimental/Research          |

Note: 127.x.x.x is reserved for loopback (localhost), so it is not assigned to devices on a network.

