Class D

Used for Multicast.

Example:

239.1.1.1

Instead of sending data to one computer:

Server ---> PC1

or everyone:

Server ---> Entire Network

Multicast sends to only devices that joined the multicast group:

        Server
           |
   -----------------
   |       |       |
 PC1      PC2     PC3
          (Joined Group)

Only PC2 receives the multicast traffic.

Common uses:

Live video streaming
IPTV
Video conferencing
Routing protocol updates
Class E

Range:

240.0.0.0 – 255.255.255.254

Reserved for:

Research
Experimental networking

These addresses are generally not used on normal networks.

Private IP Address Ranges

These are reserved for internal networks and are not routable on the public Internet.

Class	Private Range
A	10.0.0.0 – 10.255.255.255
B	172.16.0.0 – 172.31.255.255
C	192.168.0.0 – 192.168.255.255

