A few important special addresses to remember
127.0.0.1 — Loopback (localhost), used to test your own computer's network stack.
0.0.0.0 — Represents "this network" or an unspecified address; you'll often see it as a default route or when a device doesn't yet have an IP address.
255.255.255.255 — Limited broadcast address, used to send a packet to all devices on the local network.
